@startuml
title API console - one create operation per process
actor Operator
participant "API console process" as CLI
participant ApiConsole as Command
participant SmurfsApiClient as Client
participant "Smurfs.API catalog endpoint" as API
participant "Server Create.Handler" as Create
Operator -> CLI : createsmurf --name ...
CLI -> Command : CreateAsync(options)
ref over Command : Load environment override or endpoint-scoped saved token
alt token missing
  Command --> Operator : Authentication error, exit 1 (no prompt)
else token available
  Command -> Client : UseAccessToken(token)
  Command -> Client : CreateSmurfAsync(name)
  Client -> API : POST /api/smurfs {name}\nAuthorization: Bearer token
  alt validated and committed
    API -> Create : Send Create.Command
    Create -> Create : Validate, generate entity, commit
    Create --> API : Success
    API --> Client : 200
    Client --> Command : Completed
    Command --> Operator : Creation confirmation, exit 0
  else validation failure / rejected token / forbidden
    API --> Client : 400 / 401 / 403
    Client --> Command : ApiException
    Command --> Operator : Error on stderr, exit 1
  else transport failure / unconfirmed HTTP outcome
    Client --> Command : Exception
    Command --> Operator : Check list before trying again, exit 1
  end
end
note over CLI
  No automatic login, POST retry, or list reload.
  Correction/retry requires a new explicit invocation.
end note
@enduml
